1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,639
An atom that loses or gains electrons becomes a charged ion.

2
00:00:03,639 --> 00:00:08,114
Metals lose electrons to form positive ions, or cations: sodium loses one.

3
00:00:08,114 --> 00:00:12,827
Non-metals gain electrons to form negative ions, or anions: chlorine gains one.

4
00:00:13,886 --> 00:00:20,210
Opposite charges attract. This electrostatic attraction between oppositely charged ions is an ionic bond,

5
00:00:20,210 --> 00:00:22,418
forming sodium chloride: table salt.

6
00:00:22,418 --> 00:00:27,966
Magnesium loses two electrons, so it bonds with two chloride ions to make magnesium chloride.
